      "standardized_narrative": "Using the detailed gross claims development triangle, the syndicate experienced a gross prior-year release of c. GBP 28.2m (4.7% of opening gross claims reserves) in 2023. The release reflected favourable claims development across multiple classes (notably long-tail casualty and motor/auto), partially offset by deterioration in some prior catastrophe-exposed years (notably 2020 wind events). Named large losses (Hurricane Ian 2022, Hurricane Ida 2021, 2020 wind events) and the Covid-19 provision were highlighted in the report; the net reported surplus after reinsurance was GBP 23.0m.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "due to higher than expected incurred movements across most classes of business.",
